index 31fe1b1..b7c8f75 100644
--- a/patches/README.md
+++ b/patches/README.md
@@ -345,3 +345,7 @@ Reserved:
   0198 fixes the Privacy Screen dimming nothing in Chrome (owner, 2026-11-12): a focused item that fills the screen, such as a web page, made the clear band the whole screen. `PrivacyBand` now centres the band on the visible part of the focused item and keeps it to a third of the screen (or the minimum band, if more); `SablePrivacy` logs each switch and a shade that fails to show.
   0199 fits the home's Hub and Command to the Q25 (owner, 2026-11-12: Hub "looks good on Titan 2 but doesn't scale well on the Q25"). In a short window, as the Q25 column of the approved TenSeven BB10 design review: Material's 45 sp display title becomes 26 sp and the Hub title 22 sp; the upcoming-calendar row is a flat 13 sp line instead of a card; message rows are 7 dp tighter with 24 dp icons; the selected message in Notification options shows one line; Command has less padding. The Titan 2 layout is unchanged. The BB10 home bar keeps a Command (search) icon before Camera, which the compact policy dropped on the Q25; `q25_fit` checks it.
   0200 lays Sable Calendar out as TenSeven Launcher's Calendar (owner, 2026-11-12): a top bar with ‹ title › ("Today · Nov 13", "Nov 9 – Nov 15", "November 2026"), Calendars (▤) and a ⋮ menu with Search and Today; a seven-day strip with the chosen day filled blue; and Today · Week · Month · Day · + tabs instead of the action bar. The big "calendar" header, the identity mark and the month over the agenda are gone; Month keeps the busy rings and lists the chosen day under it; Week shows seven days. The key hints are hidden in a short window. `CalendarChrome` holds the titles, steps and strip (CalendarChromeTest); 6 new strings in all 19 languages.
+  0201 keeps every Sable app between the status bar and the navigation or gesture bar (owner, 2026-11-13: Calendar's top bar ran under the status bar on the Q25). Android 15+ draws apps edge to edge, and Calendar, Browser, Notes, Tasks, Weather and Text Reader did not pad for the bars; `SableGlobalTheme` with a window now pads its content for the safe drawing area (bars, cutout, keyboard) and paints the theme background behind the bars, so apps that already pad find the insets used. Calendar follows TenSeven Launcher's Calendar more closely (owner photos 2026-11-13): Week is a list of the seven days with "Mon, Nov 9 · 2 events" and their events (all-day events placed by their UTC date), Month has smaller rings on the Q25 with the week strip and the day's events under it, and the strip marks days with events with a dot. Strings `one_event` and `n_events` come in all 19 languages.
+  0202 adds a **Darkness** setting to the Privacy Screen (owner, 2026-11-13): Dim, Dark (the default, as before) or Black, from the service's settings in Accessibility or by holding the Quick Settings tile. The shade changes at once while it is up.
+  0203 drops "Select a notification icon" from the home's lock layer when there are no notifications (owner photo and UI dump, 2026-11-13), so it is just the clock and date; the hint returns with the first notification icon. `quiet_lock` checks it.
+  0204 is the Q25 type audit (owner, 2026-11-13): the shared Sable type scale defined only 8 of Material's 15 text roles, so `displayMedium`, `displaySmall`, `headlineSmall`, `titleSmall`, `bodySmall`, `labelMedium` and `labelSmall` (used by Calendar, Hub, Messages, Notes, Media, Assistant, Browser and Games) fell back to Material's sizes in Roboto. Every role now uses Source Sans 3 at a Sable size, with a Q25 size in short windows; the Q25 screen title (`displayLarge`) is 24 sp instead of 28 sp, as the TenSeven Q25 column. Weather's current temperature and picture are 56 sp and 72 dp on the Q25 (84 sp and 104 dp elsewhere).
